# Trivy ignores for the DraftCourt analytics image (services/analytics/Dockerfile).
#
# Time-bounded risk acceptance per BUILD_SPEC §13 ("Address critical/high
# vulnerabilities before deploy or record a time-bounded risk acceptance").
#
# Basis: trivy 0.70.0 image scan, 2026-09-08, AFTER `apt-get upgrade` in the
# Dockerfile (python:3.12.5-slim stays pinned; only Debian packages move).
# Every CVE listed below has NO fixed version in Debian bookworm at scan
# time (trivy status affected / fix_deferred / will_not_fix, empty
# FixedVersion) — there is nothing left to upgrade to on this base.
#
# Scope of acceptance: the analytics service is INTERNAL-ONLY (no browser
# traffic; service-auth bearer + timestamp window per
# docs/architecture/06-trust-boundaries.md). The findings sit in base-image
# OS packages (util-linux mount helpers, perl-base regex, ncurses, sqlite
# libs, expat, zlib MiniZip) that the Python service does not invoke as
# setuid/helper binaries. Production is unprovisioned (see
# docs/architecture/05-deployment-topology.md); revisit before any public
# deploy and on/before the expiry below.
#
# Mechanism: one CVE per line with machine-enforced expiry (exp:YYYY-MM-DD).
# CVEs NOT listed here still fail the CI gate. Re-scan with
# `trivy image --severity HIGH,CRITICAL` and drop entries that gain fixes.
CVE-2023-45853 exp:2026-12-08
